UID:a4-residency-chengdu-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T085306Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261231
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
SUMMARY:Deadline: A4 Residency Art Center: International Residency Fellowsh
 ip 2028 (Chengdu)
DESCRIPTION:The A4 Residency Art Center in Chengdu\, the residency platform
  of the A4 Art Museum in Luxelakes Eco-City\, opens its full-year 2028 rec
 ruitment. The interdisciplinary\, open and collaborative platform fosters 
 creative exchange among artists\, scientists\, writers and other professio
 nals\, with residents initiating participatory local activities that conne
 ct them with the city and community\; A4 also organises group activities\,
  sharing sessions\, media promotion and exhibition opportunities. CYCLES: 
 Spring 2028 (April to June) and Autumn 2028 (July to October)\, each appro
 ximately eight weeks. WHAT YOU GET (International Residency Fellowship\, f
 ully funded): private studio and accommodation\, round-trip economy airfar
 e or second-class train within a set budget\, a production grant of RMB 10
 \,000 per person or team for materials and production (excluding living ex
 penses)\, community engagement and cultural experiences\, media promotion 
 and networking. ELIGIBILITY: multidisciplinary creators worldwide\, includ
 ing visual and performing artists\, musicians\, filmmakers\, architects\, 
 curators\, designers and creatives with interdisciplinary backgrounds brid
 ging art\, business and culture. APPLICATION: free\; submit a photo\, port
 folio\, CV and project proposal in English and Chinese to a4residency@a4am
 .cn\, with the subject line specifying the programme tier and preferred cy
 cle. DEADLINE: 31 December 2026 for the 2028 full-year recruitment. A para
 llel self-funded light track exists\; this listing covers the funded fello
 wship only.\n\nOrganisation: A4 Residency Art Center (A4 Art Museum)\nLoca
 tion: Luxelakes Eco-City\, Tianfu New Area\, Chengdu\, China. Open worldwi
 de.\nAward: Fully funded fellowship: private studio and accommodation\, ro
 und-trip economy airfare or second-class train ticket within a set budget\
 , and a production grant of RMB 10\,000 per person/team for materials and 
 production (excluding living expenses). No application fee.\nDuration: App
 roximately 8 weeks\, in the Spring 2028 (April to June) or Autumn 2028 (Ju
 ly to October) cycle.\n\nMore: https://www.a4artmuseum.com/en/a4-residency
 artcenter/residing/latest-recruitment/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.a4artmuseum.com/en/a4-residencyartcenter/residing/latest-re
 cruitment/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Luxelakes Eco-City\, Tianfu New Area\, Chengdu\, China. Open world
 wide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:impart-nalli-fellowships-2027-28@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T085306Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: The Impart & Nalli Fellowships 2027-28
DESCRIPTION:A research fellowship from Impart\, an online platform building
  accessible resources on South Asia's art histories\, in collaboration wit
 h Nalli Silks\, a heritage textile brand established in 1928. The programm
 e has supported two research projects a year since 2024-25\; for the 2027-
 28 cycle two fellowships are awarded\, each carrying a grant of up to INR 
 5.5 lakhs for one year of independent research and project development. AR
 EAS OF FOCUS: underexplored textile-related histories\, practices and trad
 itions across South Asia. Any textile-centric subject may be proposed\; th
 e call particularly encourages textiles in religious\, literary\, liturgic
 al and mythological contexts\; the environmental impact of textile product
 ion and consumption\; endangered or disappearing textile traditions\; crit
 ical perspectives on textile revivalism\, digitisation\, archives and mate
 rial afterlives\; labour in textile production with attention to caste\, c
 lass and gender\; relationships between textiles and other cultural forms 
 including storytelling\, poetry\, music\, architecture and material cultur
 e\; techniques\, technologies and tools tied to specific traditions\; Sout
 h Asian textiles within the contemporary global design economy\; intellect
 ual property\, ownership and cultural rights\; and socio-cultural perspect
 ives on the relationship between handmade and industrial textiles. ELIGIBI
 LITY: open to anyone aged 18 or over residing anywhere in the world\, prov
 ided the project engages with textile practices in the wider South Asia re
 gion (Afghanistan\, Bangladesh\, Bhutan\, India\, the Maldives\, Myanmar\,
  Nepal\, Pakistan\, Sri Lanka\, Tibet). Early- and mid-career researchers\
 , designers\, archivists\, journalists\, writers\, educators\, practitione
 rs\, collectives and small organisations are all welcome\, and collaborati
 ve projects are permitted provided co-creators are credited and listed in 
 the application. Both new and ongoing projects are eligible\, but applican
 ts must specify which part of the project the grant will develop and discl
 ose any current or previous funding from other organisations. SUPPORTED FO
 RMATS: journalistic inquiry\, documentary film\, archive activation\, prac
 tice-based research\, archive generation\, digitisation and documentation 
 initiatives\, and exhibition or book projects. DELIVERABLES: a comprehensi
 ve project report at the end of the grant period\; a research dossier deve
 loped from that report in collaboration with Impart\, presenting key quest
 ions and findings and hosted on Impart's website for public benefit\; and 
 a set of final project outputs\, which may be audio-visual (interviews\, s
 hort films)\, visual essays (photographic or process-based documentation)\
 , written pieces (essays\, features\, interviews) or curatorial work (exhi
 bition or digital curation). Fellows also take part in periodic check-ins 
 and submit progress reports. Copyright is settled case by case\, but all f
 inal outputs must be made openly and freely accessible to the public. APPL
 ICATION: a Google Form structured as a full project proposal\, plus a proj
 ect budget (percentage-based allocation is acceptable\, but be as specific
  as possible)\, a project timeline for the one-year period with key phases
 \, activities and milestones\, and a single supporting PDF containing an u
 p-to-date CV\, selected work samples\, and up to two letters of support or
  recommendation. The form is in English\; applicants who would prefer anot
 her language are invited to write to Impart to arrange an alternative. NOT
 E: the fellowship has a strict no-tolerance policy on the use of AI or LLM
 s in the application form or any submitted materials\, and any violation r
 esults in rejection. KEY DATES: applications close 31 August 2026\; awarde
 es notified December 2026\; fellowships run January to December 2027. No i
 ndividual feedback is given on unsuccessful applications.\n\nOrganisation:
  Impart in collaboration with Nalli Silks\nLocation: Remote and self-direc
 ted\; applicants may reside anywhere in the world. Projects must engage wi
 th textile practices across South Asia: Afghanistan\, Bangladesh\, Bhutan\
 , India\, the Maldives\, Myanmar\, Nepal\, Pakistan\, Sri Lanka and Tibet.
 \nAward: Up to INR 5.5 lakhs (INR 550\,000) per fellow towards project exe
 cution\, covering research-related expenses including travel\, fieldwork a
 nd documentation subject to approval. Two fellowships are awarded. No appl
 ication fee.\nDuration: One year\, January to December 2027\n\nMore: https
 ://imp-art.org/fellowship-grant/impart-x-nalli-fellowships/?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://imp-art.org/fellowship-grant/impart-x-nalli-fellowships/?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote and self-directed\; applicants may reside anywhere in the w
 orld. Projects must engage with textile practices across South Asia: Afgha
 nistan\, Bangladesh\, Bhutan\, India\, the Maldives\, Myanmar\, Nepal\, Pa
 kistan\, Sri Lanka and Tibet.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:acc-new-york-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T085306Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261111
SUMMARY:Deadline: Asian Cultural Council New York Fellowship 2027 (USD 38\,
 000)
DESCRIPTION:The Asian Cultural Council's New York Fellowship brings artists
 \, scholars and arts professionals from Asia to New York City for a six-mo
 nth immersive cultural exchange. SUPPORT: USD 38\,000 for the six-month fe
 llowship. ELIGIBILITY: non-US citizens/residents from ACC-eligible Asian c
 ountries (including Bangladesh\, Cambodia\, China\, Hong Kong\, India\, In
 donesia\, Japan\, Korea\, Malaysia\, Mongolia\, Myanmar\, Nepal\, Pakistan
 \, Philippines\, Singapore\, Sri Lanka\, Taiwan\, Thailand and Vietnam\, a
 mong others)\; age 21+\; at least five years of professional experience in
  an eligible discipline (architecture\, archaeology\, art history\, arts a
 dministration\, arts criticism\, conservation\, crafts\, curation\, dance\
 , ethnomusicology\, film\, literature\, museum studies\, music\, theater\,
  visual art)\; English proficiency (J-1 visa requirement)\; fellows cannot
  work or pursue coursework during the fellowship. COHORTS: January-June 20
 28 or July-December 2028. HOW TO APPLY: via the GoApply platform\; applica
 tions open 1 October 2026. Recommendation letters due 16 November 2026. No
  application fee. DEADLINE: 10 November 2026 at 9:59 AM ET.\n\nOrganisatio
 n: Asian Cultural Council\nLocation: Six-month fellowship in New York City
 . For artists\, scholars and arts professionals from ACC-eligible Asian co
 untries (non-US citizens/residents).\nAward: USD 38\,000 for the six-month
  fellowship\, covering the immersive cultural exchange in New York City. N
 o application fee.\nDuration: Six months\, in one of two cohorts: January-
 June 2028 or July-December 2028\n\nMore: https://www.asianculturalcouncil.
 org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
URL:https://www.asianculturalcouncil.org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Six-month fellowship in New York City. For artists\, scholars and 
 arts professionals from ACC-eligible Asian countries (non-US citizens/resi
 dents).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:acc-individual-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261025T085306Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261111
SUMMARY:Deadline: Asian Cultural Council Individual Fellowship 2027 (up to 
 USD 35\,000)
DESCRIPTION:The Asian Cultural Council's Individual Fellowship supports sel
 f-directed exploration and cultural exchange experiences in a new or less 
 familiar environment\, fostering exchange between the United States and As
 ia and within Asia. SUPPORT: up to USD 35\,000 for a 1-to-6-month program 
 (minimum 30 days\; two or more months preferred)\; single or joint applica
 tions with up to 3 participants. ELIGIBILITY: citizens or permanent reside
 nts of ACC-eligible countries (the US and countries across Asia\, from Afg
 hanistan to Vietnam)\; age 21+\; at least five years of professional exper
 ience in an eligible discipline (architecture\, archaeology\, art history\
 , arts administration\, arts criticism\, conservation\, crafts\, curation\
 , dance\, ethnomusicology\, film\, literature\, museum studies\, music\, t
 heater\, visual art)\; English proficiency if traveling to the US\; no cou
 rsework or teaching during the fellowship. Grant activities must take plac
 e between 1 August 2027 and 31 December 2028. HOW TO APPLY: via the GoAppl
 y platform\; applications open 1 October 2026. Recommendation letters due 
 16 November 2026. No application fee. DEADLINE: 10 November 2026 at 9:59 A
 M ET.\n\nOrganisation: Asian Cultural Council\nLocation: Self-directed cul
 tural exchange between the US and Asia\, or within Asia. For citizens and 
 permanent residents of ACC-eligible countries (including the US).\nAward: 
 Up to USD 35\,000 for self-directed exploration and cultural exchange of 1
  to 6 months. Single or joint applications (up to 3 participants). No appl
 ication fee.\nDuration: 1 to 6 months (minimum 30 days\; 2 or more months 
 preferred)\, with grant activities between 1 August 2027 and 31 December 2
 028\n\nMore: https://www.asianculturalcouncil.org/grant-opportunities?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.asianculturalcouncil.org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Self-directed cultural exchange between the US and Asia\, or withi
 n Asia. For citizens and permanent residents of ACC-eligible countries (in
 cluding the US).
END:VEVENT
